[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-craft-fabrication-decision :finalize-carving-decision :proceed-with-craft-fabrication :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage" "2799007318-cloud-itonami-isco-7318-handicraft-workers-textile-leather-coverage" "2799007222-cloud-itonami-isco-7222-toolmakers-coverage" "2799009311-cloud-itonami-isco-9311-mining-quarrying-labourers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the craft-fabrication work" "proceed with the carving work" "proceed with the weaving work" "finalize the craft-fabrication decision" "finalize the carving decision" "finalize the weaving decision" "override the workshop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override workshop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007317, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :handicraft/wood-basketry-workshop-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:worker-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7317", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007317: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7317 Handicraft Workers in Wood, Basketry and Related Materials workshop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7317\n-- Handicraft Workers in Wood, Basketry and Related Materials** only,\nWave3 (production/trades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7317\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7317\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Handicraft Workers in Wood,\nBasketry and Related Materials\" -- confirming the premise, no\nmismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7317` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7317` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nHandicraft Workers in Wood, Basketry and Related Materials use hand\ntools and cutting equipment on natural fiber/wood materials -- real\nphysical-safety stakes (cut hazards, dust exposure, repetitive-strain\ninjury). The controlling constraint for this vertical is that the\nclosed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes\na craft-fabrication-execution decision (e.g. deciding to proceed with\na specific carving, weaving or finishing step), or overrides a\nworkshop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a\nhard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-\neligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to WORKSHOP\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs the craft\nfabrication work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, itself modeled closely on\ncloud-itonami-isco-9311's physical-safety-domain shape) -- cloned and\nread in full in this session. Its build (`clojure -M:test`) was\nre-verified locally during this session and remains green, and its\n`deps.edn` `langgraph` git-sha pin was cross-checked against the most\nrecently created sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-6224` (created the same\nday as this ADR) and found identical, confirming the pin is still\ncurrent across the fleet. The adjacent registry entry `{:id \"7318\"\n...}` (Handicraft Workers in Textile, Leather and Related Materials)\nwas inspected for naming disambiguation only -- it is `:implemented`\nunder a different, production-execution-shaped operating-state\nsequence (`:intake :craft :finish :deliver :invoice :audit`) not\nmirrored here, since this task's explicit domain design is\ncoordination-only (`:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit`,\nmatching this entry's own registry `:operating-states`).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7317` as an OSS workshop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for wood-and-basketry\nhandicraft workshops, following the SAME governed-actor architecture\nas every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Wood &\nBasketry Handicraft Workshop Advisor ⊣ WoodBasketryGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct craft-fabrication-execution\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising a craft-fabrication-execution\ndecision (e.g. a specific carving, weaving or finishing step), or any\noverride of a workshop safety officer's judgment. These are not\nmerely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent from\nthe op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a cut-hazard/dust-exposure/\n  repetitive-strain-injury concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- wood/basketry-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\ncraft-fabrication-execution decision or a workshop-safety-officer-\njudgment override. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-craft-fabrication-decision` cannot even be proposed\nby the reference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions\nonly ever emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`woodbasketry.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-craft-fabrication-decision`, `:finalize-carving-decision`,\n`:proceed-with-craft-fabrication`, `:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and\nis verified by dedicated unit tests\n(`woodbasketry.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-craft-fabrication-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-carving-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Worker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered worker record (`:no-worker`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the worker is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop (`:no-workshop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/workshop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the five\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with\n   craft-fabrication work, or overriding a workshop safety officer's\n   judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks craft-fabrication-execution/safety-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a cut-hazard/dust-\n  exposure/repetitive-strain-injury observation -- it never resolves\n  the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about workshop safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  wood/basketry-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  craft-fabrication-execution or safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"craft\", \"wood\", \"basketry\", \"carving\", \"weaving\", \"safety\") can\naccidentally match inside the mock advisor's own default rationale\ntext for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy\npath -- this is exactly the risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a\nworkshop coordination actor working adjacent to carving/weaving work\nnecessarily discusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job)\ncould trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`woodbasketry.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\ncraft-fabrication work\", \"finalize the weaving decision\", \"override\nthe workshop safety officer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own\nworked example phrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`woodbasketry.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for worker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nbasketry-weaving task ...\", \"... routed for workshop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`woodbasketry.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7317\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7317` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7317`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-carving-decision` or\n  `:approve-weaving-decision` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for\n  `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means\n  the *capability* to finalize a craft-fabrication-execution decision\n  exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For\n  a decision this severe (cut hazards, dust exposure, repetitive-\n  strain injury), the capability itself must not exist. The only op\n  related to workshop-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`,\n  which surfaces the need for human/workshop-safety-officer attention\n  and never itself decides, authorizes, or defers a\n  craft-fabrication-execution decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold wood/basketry-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the craft-fabrication-\n  execution/safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional\n  block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"craft\" \"wood\"\n  \"basketry\" \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known\n  self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked\n  example for this exact task), and per the explicit instruction to\n  phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS,\n  never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  craft/wood/basketry/safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `worker` and `workshop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered worker AND independently-registered\n  workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/workshop\n  record must be independently verified/registered before any action\"\n  and the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered worker AND\n   workshop (`:no-worker`/`:no-workshop`). Not a\n   craft-fabrication-execution or safety-officer decision in any\n   respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a craft-fabrication-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific carving, weaving or finishing step -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a cut-hazard/dust-exposure/\n   repetitive-strain-injury concern to a human/workshop safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the workshop\n   safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- wood/basketry-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a\n   craft-fabrication-execution or authorization decision of any kind\n   -- it is a purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary\n   cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na craft-fabrication-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a\nspecific carving, weaving or finishing step) or a\nworkshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`woodbasketry.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`woodbasketry.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`woodbasketry.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-craft-fabrication-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-carving-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`woodbasketry.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with craft-fabrication work or override a\nworkshop safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted\nop\n(`woodbasketry.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Wood & Basketry Handicraft Workshop Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :worker-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7317", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7317", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7317], :test/simulator :woodbasketry.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7317 — Handicraft Workers in Wood, Basketry and Related Materials Workshop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7317}]